From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:27:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: read the reset back on the A10X only

The reset read-back was written and run on the J120 (A10X). On every
other SoC a reset state that does not read back as requested would now
fail the reset where it succeeded before, so check it on the T8011 only
until other SoCs have been tried. Register access errors are still
returned everywhere; the MMIO regmap does not produce them.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
index 0499a5b43..3a46a5341 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@ struct apple_pmgr_ps {
 	u32 min_state;
 	bool has_genpd;
 	bool manual_pm;
+	/* Read the reset back; checked on the A10X only so far */
+	bool verify_reset;
 };
 
 #define genpd_to_apple_pmgr_ps(_genpd) container_of(_genpd, struct apple_pmgr_ps, genpd)
@@ -201,6 +203,9 @@ static int apple_pmgr_reset_verify(struct apple_pmgr_ps *ps, bool asserted)
 	u32 val;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!ps->verify_reset)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = regmap_read(ps->regmap, ps->offset, &val);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
@@ -324,6 +329,7 @@ static int apple_pmgr_ps_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ps->dev = dev;
 	ps->regmap = regmap;
+	ps->verify_reset = of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8011");
 	spin_lock_init(&ps->lock);
 
 	ret = of_property_read_string(node, "label", &name);
